Hi,

while trying to debug a hibernation/rtc_cmos alarm wakeup problem in 
2.6.22 (or later) I noticed that the latest kernel crashes (or gets 
stuck sometimes) during boot after the message:

SMP alternatives: switching to UP code

Every kernel up to 2.6.22.1 works fine on the system. I've attached the 
log file taken from the serial console (4 boot attempts with different 
acpi= options) and the .config of the kernel. The kernel is from the 
Fedora 8 development line.

BTW: While this is a Fedora 8 kernel I had the same problem with a plain 
2.6.23-rc3 kernel with the latest suspend/hibernate patches applied.

Is there any more information I should collect and attach in further 
postings?

Please include my e-mail address in the CC as I'm not subscribing to 
this list.

Regards,

	Stefan

---
Stefan Becker
